Jirin represents the monk's heightened awareness and reflexive defensive
abilities. Through intensive training, monks develop an almost supernatural
sense for incoming attacks, allowing them to dodge and block with uncanny
precision.

Unlike the thief's Dodge skill which relies on anticipating attacks, Jirin
operates through pure instinct and bodily awareness. The monk's body simply
moves out of harm's way before the conscious mind registers the threat.

This passive skill activates automatically during combat. Higher skill levels
increase both the frequency and effectiveness of defensive reactions. Masters
of Jirin can deflect blows that would fell lesser warriors while barely
seeming to move.

Class: Monk
Discipline: Mind Body

